[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Make the tree-sitter grammar parse standalone .sgra files

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[SPIKE]
UID: SPIKE-SGRA-PARSE
TITLE: Make the tree-sitter grammar parse standalone .sgra files
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: run
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A three-rule patch is applied and the two .sgra files parse with no regression
across the sdoc corpus.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The upstream tree-sitter grammar parses all sdoc documents but fails every
standalone .sgra grammar file, because its root rule requires a DOCUMENT header.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Run. The DOCUMENT-header fix alone was not sufficient: our own grammar.sgra
also uses REVERSE_ROLE on every non-File Parent relation, and upstream's
grammar_relation_parent/child rules had no field for it at all, so it still
errored after the root-rule fix. The applied patch is therefore three rule
changes across two files (source_file's root choice, a new standalone_grammar
rule, and REVERSE_ROLE added to both relation rules) rather than one.

Measured against this repo's own corpus (6 .sdoc + grammar.sgra): 6/7 clean
before the patch, 7/7 after. Measured against strictdoc-project/strictdoc's
own docs/ (15 files, pinned rev 215cda2e): 5/15 clean both before and after —
the other 10 fail on pre-existing document-body/FREETEXT coverage gaps this
patch never targeted (out of DEC-GRAMMAR-PATCH-NOT-FORK's scope; logged as
MECH-SGRA-BODY-COVERAGE in the plan backlog). checks/strictdoc-grammar-corpus.nix
is the standing regression gate against both corpora.
<<<
